  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh Mahila Parishad (BMP) - Bangladesh Mahila Parishad</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bangladesh Mahila Parishad (BMP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incrementally contribute to reducing all forms of gender based discrimination in Bangladesh by engendering the post 2015 development agenda and keeping gender equality, women&#x2019;s empowerment and women&#x2019;s human rights at the center while upholding the basic values of human rights, democracy and good governance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xF6;d till BMP (2018 - 2022)

Bangladesh Mahila Parishad (BMP) &#xE4;r en volont&#xE4;rbaserad icke-statlig organisation i Bangladesh som arbetar f&#xF6;r kvinnors r&#xE4;ttigheter. Organisationen bildades i Dhaka 1970 f&#xF6;r att arbeta f&#xF6;r kvinnors frig&#xF6;relse. BMP har mer &#xE4;n 150 000 medlemmar och mer &#xE4;n 2000 gr&#xE4;srotsniv&#xE5;kommitt&#xE9;er utspridda &#xF6;ver hela landet. Dess medlemmar kommer fr&#xE5;n alla samh&#xE4;llsskikt och best&#xE5;r av alltifr&#xE5;n utbildade professionella kvinnor till lantbruksarbetande kvinnor.

BMP: s f&#xF6;reslagna projekt f&#xF6;r perioden 2018-2022 syftar till att gradvis bidra till att minska alla former av k&#xF6;nsbaserad diskriminering i Bangladesh genom att implementera genderfr&#xE5;gor i utvecklingsagendan efter 2015.

Det finns tre huvudm&#xE5;l som programmet kommer att arbeta f&#xF6;r att uppn&#xE5;:
1. Fr&#xE4;mja och skydda kvinnors m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter, motst&#xE5; alla former av v&#xE5;ld mot kvinnor och flickor.
2. Fr&#xE4;mjande av kvinnors m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och arbeta f&#xF6;r effektivt och meningsfullt deltagande av kvinnor i politiska processer och beslutsfattande f&#xF6;r att st&#xE4;rka demokratin och god samh&#xE4;llsstyrning
3. F&#xF6;rst&#xE4;rkning och konsolidering av BMP: s kapacitet

Sverige har indikativt beslutat om st&#xF6;d till projektet med en sammanlagd summa p&#xE5; 25 000 000 kronor.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to BMP (2018 - 2022)

Bangladesh Mahila Parishad (BMP) is a volunteer-based non-governmental organization in Bangladesh working for women&#x2019;s rights. The organisation was established in Dhaka in 1970 to work for the emancipation of women. BMP has more than 150,000 members and more than 2000 grassroots level committees spread all over the country. Its members come from all walks of life and consist of urban educated professional women to the rural agricultural workers.

BMP&apos;s proposed project for the period 2018-2022 aims to incrementally contribute to reduce all forms of gender based discrimination in Bangladesh by engendering the post 2015 development agenda.

There are three main objectives that the programme will work towards:
1. Promote and protect women&apos;s human rights, resisting all forms of violence against women and girls. 
2. Advocacy lobby for women&apos;s human rights and effective and meaningful participation of women in political process and decision making towards strengthening democracy and good governance 
3. Strengthening and consolidating capacity of BMP

Sweden has indicated support to the Project with a total allocation of SEK 25 000 000.</narrative>
  </description>
